# Room Write-up: Nmap Basics
**Platform:** TryHackMe | **Module:** Network Security

## 🎯 Objective
Learn the fundamentals of network scanning using Nmap to discover live hosts, open ports, and running services.

## 🛠️ Key Commands & Syntax
```bash
# Basic TCP SYN Scan (Stealth Scan)
nmap -sS -T4 <target_ip>

# Comprehensive Scan (Version detection, OS detection, default scripts, all ports)
nmap -sV -O -sC -p- <target_ip>
🔍 Methodology & Steps

    Host Discovery: Ping sweep or default scan to check which IP addresses are active on the target network.

    Port Scanning: Used -sS to scan for open ports without completing the full TCP 3-way handshake, minimizing detection risk.

    Service Enumeration: Applied -sV to probe open ports and determine the exact software versions running behind them.

    Script Scanning: Ran Nmap Scripting Engine (-sC) to check for common misconfigurations or vulnerabilities.

💡 Key Takeaways

    Always match your scan timing template (-T0 to -T5) to the network environment to avoid crashing fragile systems or triggering loud alarms.

    Service version detection is the critical first step before looking up potential exploits.
